body:
`handleEditorChange` returns early when `value` is an empty string (`if (!value) return;`). Because the Monaco `Editor` is controlled via `value={editorValue}`, this prevents users from clearing the editor (it will snap back to the previous value) and also skips updating error state. Change the guard to only ignore `undefined` and handle `''` by setting an appropriate error (and/or clearing the preview).
```suggestion
    // Ignore undefined (no update), but handle empty string as an actual value
    if (value === undefined) return;

    setEditorValue(value);

    // If the editor is empty (or only whitespace), set an error and skip parsing
    if (value.trim() === '') {
      setError('Editor is empty. Please provide a valid JSON schema.');
      return;
    }
```

The parsed JSON is assigned directly to `schema` without validating that it's an object with a `type`. If a user enters a primitive like `true` or `1`, `SchemaRenderer` will throw at runtime when accessing `schema.type`, which will break the whole playground. Add a runtime check before calling `setSchema` (e.g., ensure `parsed` is a non-null object and `typeof (parsed as any).type === 'string'`), otherwise set an error and skip rendering.
```suggestion

      // Validate that the parsed value is a schema-like object before rendering
      if (
        parsed !== null &&
        typeof parsed === 'object' &&
        typeof (parsed as any).type === 'string'
      ) {
        setSchema(parsed as SchemaNode);
        setError(null);
      } else {
        setError('Schema must be a JSON object with a string "type" property.');
      }
```
